#!/usr/bin/env etcs
#IMPORT ACE_ROOT/modules
# ETCS Causal Stream Demo: Cross-Instance Database Teleportation
# This script demonstrates moving structured data across isolated SQLite instances
# strictly through the LMAX causal buffer, with zero serializers or variables.
#
# LIFETIME NOTE: 'source' and 'target' are injected by the caller
# (gdata_server.etcs), which spawns and Connects both before this
# script ever runs. This script borrows them — it must never Connect,
# Disconnect, or Close either one; the caller owns their lifetime
# start to finish. As a consequence, this script is no longer safe to
# run standalone with unbound roles (see accompanying note).

requires source
requires target

# --- Phase 1: Use the already-open source connection ---
source.ExecuteRaw(PRAGMA journal_mode=WAL;)
source.InitializeSchema(CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS players(id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT, level INTEGER);)
source.ExecuteTransaction(DELETE FROM players;INSERT INTO players (name, level) VALUES('Lux', 99), ('Sibte', 100), ('Entropy', 0);)
source.ExecuteRaw(PRAGMA wal_checkpoint(FULL);)

# --- Phase 2: Use the already-open target connection ---
target.ExecuteRaw(PRAGMA journal_mode=WAL;)
# Notice we DO NOT initialize the 'players' table here.
# The causal stream will instantiate the schema on the target automatically.

# --- Phase 3: The Causal Stream ---
# Produce rows from source directly into the target's consumer.
source.QueryProduce(SELECT * FROM players) -> target.RowConsume()

# --- Phase 4: intentionally no-op ---
# source/target stay open and connected. The caller (gdata_server.etcs)
# disconnects and closes both, once, after every borrower is finished.